  "b6_reason": "Reduction of an isocyanide (CH3NC) by LiAlH4 gives a secondary amine (CH3NHCH3), not a primary amine, while the other three routes all end in CH3NH2 or CH3CH2NH2.",
  "b6_working": "1) CH3CONH2 + Br2/KOH = Hofmann bromamide degradation -> CH3NH2 (1 deg). 2) CH3CN + LiAlH4/H3O+ -> CH3CH2NH2 (1 deg). 3) CH3-N=C: + LiAlH4 adds 2[H] to the terminal carbon -> CH3-NH-CH3 (2 deg amine). 4) CH3CONH2 + LiAlH4/H3O+ -> CH3CH2NH2 (1 deg).",
